-- Board mapping (the same as the C64MEGA65 K325T port and the MEGA65 core port):
--   clk_in 50 MHz -> MMCM: 100 MHz (the framework's and core's clk_i), 200 MHz (MIG
--                    system clock), 162.7 MHz (Rockchip SPI bridge)
--   HDMI          J11 Sipeed DVI Pmod (TMDS_33; green + clock pairs inverted in M2M)
--   HyperRAM   -> DDR3 MT41K128M16 via MIG + avm_mig (the framework's G_EXT_HR mode;
--                    MIG ui_clk is the framework's hr_clk)
--   SD card    -> sd_emu (SPI-mode SDHC emulator) on the framework's back-slot SD bus,
--                    sectors served by the Rockchip (m65io) through rk_bridge
--   keyboard   -> m65kbd_emu answers the M2M keyboard protocol from the Rockchip's
--                    key matrix (rk_bridge INPUT command; USB keyboard / m65d)
--   joysticks  -> rk_bridge joyA / joyB (USB gamepads / m65d)
--   mouse      -> amiga_mouse: position counters + buttons from the bridge (INPUT bytes
--                    13..16) -> quadrature on the mouse port's direction lines, buttons on
--                    fire / pot lines (port 1 by default, as on a real A500)
--   Amiga chip / slow RAM and Kickstart: block RAM inside CORE (unchanged upstream design)
--   QNICE UART -> rk_bridge monitor channel (TCP 4510 on the Rockchip), 115200 baud
--   no audio DAC: audio is on HDMI only; RTC/I2C: not present (G_NO_I2C)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
